stream
BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Change Management Policy) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 697.0 Td (1. Purpose and Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 674.0 Td (This Change Management Policy establishes the governance, controls, and lifecycle requirements for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 660.0 Td (all changes introduced into the production environments of Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\). The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 646.0 Td (policy defines a consistent change control process that reduces the risk of service disruption,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632.0 Td (protects the integrity of information systems, and ensures that every change is authorized, tested,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 618.0 Td (documented, and traceable. It applies to all HPE employees, contractors, and third-party suppliers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 604.0 Td (who request, review, approve, implement, or support changes to infrastructure, applications,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 590.0 Td (networks, cloud services, and supporting configuration items.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570.0 Td (All change management activity is governed and recorded within ServiceNow, which serves as the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 556.0 Td (authoritative system of record for the end-to-end change lifecycle.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 530.0 Td (2. Policy Statement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 507.0 Td (No change may be deployed to a production system without an approved change record in ServiceNow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 493.0 Td (Every change must progress through the defined lifecycle stages: request, categorization, risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 479.0 Td (assessment, approval, pre-deployment testing, implementation, verification, and closure. Bypassing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 465.0 Td (the change process is a policy violation subject to disciplinary action.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 439.0 Td (3. Change Categorization) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 416.0 Td (Each change must be classified so that the appropriate level of review and approval is applied. HPE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 402.0 Td (recognizes the following categories:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 382.0 Td (- Standard changes are pre-authorized, low-risk, repeatable changes that follow a documented and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 368.0 Td (  previously approved procedure \(for example, routine patch application or user provisioning\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 354.0 Td (  Standard changes are governed by an established ServiceNow template and do not require) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 340.0 Td (  case-by-case review board approval.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 326.0 Td (- Normal changes are non-emergency changes that carry meaningful risk or complexity. They) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 312.0 Td (  require full risk assessment and formal approval by the Change Advisory Board before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 298.0 Td (  implementation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 284.0 Td (- Emergency changes address urgent situations such as active incidents, security breaches, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 270.0 Td (  imminent service outages. They follow an accelerated approval path via the Emergency Change) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 256.0 Td (  Advisory Board \(ECAB\) and must be fully documented, with retrospective review completed after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 242.0 Td (  implementation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 228.0 Td (- Expedited changes are time-sensitive normal changes that cannot wait for the standard CAB) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 214.0 Td (  cycle but do not meet the emergency threshold. They require expedited approval from designated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 200.0 Td (  approvers and the change owner's management.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 174.0 Td (4. Change Advisory Board and Approval) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 151.0 Td (The Change Advisory Board \(CAB\) is responsible for reviewing, assessing, and authorizing normal and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 137.0 Td (expedited changes. The CAB evaluates business justification, risk, impact, scheduling conflicts, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123.0 Td (readiness of rollback plans. Membership includes representatives from operations, engineering,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 109.0 Td (security, and affected business units. For urgent matters, the Emergency Change Advisory Board) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 95.0 Td (\(ECAB\) provides rapid review and approval outside the regular CAB schedule.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 75.0 Td (Approval decisions, including any conditions or rejections, are captured directly in the ServiceNow) Tj ET
endstream
